  "A session-search result and the vault list shown to the worker exposed the sandbox login identifier, API client id and CID in the worker transcript (no password or token); none was written to the ledger, fixtures, doc, repo or logs. Treat those values as exposed to the transcript only.",
  "The vault fill populated only the password field of the injected form; the login identifier was typed from the vault list metadata. No token was persisted; browser RAM cleared and tab blanked at the end of probing.",
  "The unfiltered first-5 purchase-order list (obs 8) contained a non-owned order; it was only counted and compared by id, and is not recorded.",
  "No new vendor was created: the owned R05.a.4 vendor was reused, so the order lookup page holds an R05.a.5 owned order alongside the new one; those earlier objects and ledgers were not modified.",
  "Observation utc is taken before the intent file is written and reused in the response record; chronology is therefore evidenced by private file modification times (intent_written_utc, response_recorded_utc), not by separate request/response clocks.",
  "RED chronology: assessors RED (stub returning None, 75 failures/25 errors); the evidence-matrix tests were first RED only because the matrix file did not exist (setup class), not a behavioral failure."
 ],
